The attached image (Figure 5) illustrates that Nano-11 facilitates antigen transport to draining lymph nodes. Panel A's flow cytometry plots show that Nano-11 (OVA+N11) significantly increases both the percentage and Mean Fluorescence Intensity (MFI) of OVA-positive cells, particularly in migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs), within draining lymph nodes on Day 1 and Day 2, compared to soluble OVA or OVA+AH. Panel B quantitatively confirms higher OVA MFI with Nano-11. Panel C further highlights that Nano-11 significantly increases the percentage of MigDCs among OVA-positive cells, indicating specific targeting to these immunopotentiating cells.